Package: metaMultiverse
Type: Package
Title: Multiverse Meta-Analysis Toolkit
Version: 0.4.0
Date: 2026-09-17
Authors@R: person(given = c("Constantin", "Yves"),
                  family = "Plessen",
                  email = "constantin.plessen@uni-graz.at",
                  role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
                  comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-4907-3505",
                              affiliation = "Psychotherapy and Psychotherapy Research (CBT), Center for Psychotherapy, University of Graz"))
Description: A toolkit for multiverse meta-analysis: generate specification
    grids over study-selection and analytic decisions, estimate every
    specification (REML, Paule-Mandel, Hartung-Knapp/Sidik-Jonkman, PET-PEESE,
    p-uniform*, UWLS, WAAP, three-level and robust variance models), and
    visualize the results as specification curves and vibration-of-effects
    plots. Decisions are declared as named forks with a ruling (equivalent,
    uncertain, changes the question, indefensible) and a required
    justification; question-changing decisions define estimand cells that
    are never pooled, and an attrition ledger records every specification
    that could not be estimated. Effect sizes can be computed from arm-level
    pre/post data with the metric varied as a further decision.
